.TH ORO-INTERNAL-PERMISSIONS 3 "" "Oro Runtime" "Oro Runtime API Manual"
.SH NAME
oro:internal/permissions \- JavaScript API module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
import * as module from 'oro:internal/permissions'
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
This module provides an API for querying and requesting permissions.
.SH REFERENCE
.TP
\fBconstructor(name, initialState, options)\fR
`PermissionStatus` class constructor.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIname\fR (string; required)
.br
\fIinitialState\fR (string; required)
.br
\fIoptions\fR (object; optional)
.br
\fIoptions.signal\fR (?AbortSignal; optional; default null)
.TP
\fBname()\fR
The name of this permission this status is for.
.TP
\fBstate()\fR
The current state of the permission status.
.TP
\fBonchange()\fR
Level 0 event target 'change' event listener accessor
.TP
\fBquery(descriptor, options)\fR
Query for a permission status. The Android\-only `local\-network` permission reports access to LAN hosts. On Android versions or app targets below API 37 it is already granted.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIdescriptor\fR (PermissionDescriptor; required)
.br
\fIoptions\fR (object; optional)
.br
\fIoptions.signal\fR (?AbortSignal; optional; default null)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<PermissionStatus>\fR
.TP
\fBrequest(descriptor, options)\fR
Request a permission to be granted. Request Android's `local\-network` permission before connecting to LAN hosts. This requires Android 17 with target SDK 37 or newer, and the generated ACCESS_LOCAL_NETWORK manifest permission. Older versions need no prompt.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIdescriptor\fR (PermissionDescriptor; required)
.br
\fIoptions\fR (object; optional)
.br
\fIoptions.signal\fR (?AbortSignal; optional; default null)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<PermissionStatus>\fR
